1
00:00:03,270 --> 00:00:04,970
<i>In this world...</i>

2
00:00:05,440 --> 00:00:10,740
<i>Is the destiny of mankind controlled by some transcendental entity or law?</i>

3
00:00:11,610 --> 00:00:14,580
<i>Is it like the hand of God hovering above?</i>

4
00:00:15,680 --> 00:00:17,450
<i>At least it is true...</i>

5
00:00:17,890 --> 00:00:21,690
<i>...that man has no control, even over his own will.</i>

6
00:00:23,460 --> 00:00:25,630
Some danger always lies in the act of hunting...

7
00:00:25,630 --> 00:00:27,820
...despite the fact it is an imperial event.

8
00:00:29,430 --> 00:00:34,940
You never know what kind of
beasts hide within the woods...

9
00:00:34,940 --> 00:00:36,700
What are you trying to say?

10
00:00:36,700 --> 00:00:39,040
Of course, not only are
the beasts dangerous...

11
00:00:39,040 --> 00:00:43,340
...but so are the stray arrows that may
have been launched at the beasts.

12
00:00:43,340 --> 00:00:44,540
A stray arrow?

13
00:00:46,110 --> 00:00:50,610
And a nastily-poisoned stray arrow at that...

14
00:00:52,690 --> 00:00:54,620
If you mean...

15
00:00:55,360 --> 00:00:58,020
A stray arrow, General.

16
00:01:19,430 --> 00:01:21,510
Feel no shame about shape

17
00:01:21,600 --> 00:01:23,430
Weather changes their phrase

18
00:01:23,560 --> 00:01:27,190
Even mother will show you another way

19
00:01:27,190 --> 00:01:29,560
So put your glasses on

20
00:01:29,650 --> 00:01:31,650
Nothing will be wrong

21
00:01:31,730 --> 00:01:33,860
There's no blame. There's no fame

22
00:01:33,860 --> 00:01:35,690
It's up to you

23
00:01:35,860 --> 00:01:39,320
The first words should be found

24
00:01:39,950 --> 00:01:42,950
Whatever holds you back

25
00:01:43,830 --> 00:01:44,330
I...

26
00:01:44,700 --> 00:01:45,450
...can...

27
00:01:45,540 --> 00:01:47,620
I can get it off

28
00:01:47,620 --> 00:01:48,620
Tell me what...

29
00:01:48,620 --> 00:01:49,630
Tell me what...

30
00:01:49,630 --> 00:01:51,460
Tell me what you want

31
00:01:51,590 --> 00:01:52,550
I don't know why...

32
00:01:52,750 --> 00:01:53,550
Don't know why...

33
00:01:53,550 --> 00:01:55,550
Don't know why you're afraid

34
00:01:55,710 --> 00:01:56,720
Tell me what...

35
00:01:56,800 --> 00:01:57,680
Tell me what...

36
00:01:57,840 --> 00:01:59,340
Tell me what you'd say

37
00:01:59,590 --> 00:02:00,680
I don't know why...

38
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:01,760
Don't know why...

39
00:02:01,850 --> 00:02:02,560
Too late...

40
00:02:02,640 --> 00:02:04,180
It's too late

41
00:02:09,100 --> 00:02:13,110
Assassination

42
00:02:47,730 --> 00:02:51,400
Well, it seems they cannot
catch the quarry easily.

43
00:02:51,900 --> 00:02:55,980
Would Your Majesty like
to pursue the quarry with them?

44
00:02:55,980 --> 00:02:57,780
No, I would not.

45
00:02:57,780 --> 00:03:00,110
I'm not as young as I used to be...

46
00:03:02,530 --> 00:03:06,870
...and I'm afraid of earning their
displeasure when I carry off...

47
00:03:06,870 --> 00:03:08,700
...what they've pursued for two hours.

48
00:03:09,250 --> 00:03:11,330
It is very kind of Your Majesty.

49
00:03:39,690 --> 00:03:41,490
Look out! It's running into the brush!

50
00:03:47,790 --> 00:03:49,120
Well done, kid!

51
00:03:56,090 --> 00:03:57,710
There's no use getting sore!

52
00:04:01,300 --> 00:04:02,880
I don't get sore!

53
00:04:02,880 --> 00:04:05,140
Your feelings are written all over your face.

54
00:04:09,100 --> 00:04:12,980
Why do we have to watch
those nobles play around?

55
00:04:12,980 --> 00:04:14,100
It's ridiculous!

56
00:04:14,100 --> 00:04:15,560
We've got no choice.

57
00:04:15,560 --> 00:04:17,480
This is our duty too.

58
00:04:19,690 --> 00:04:23,450
Besides, this is easier to deal
with than fighting on some battlefield.

59
00:04:23,740 --> 00:04:24,610
That's true!

60
00:04:24,610 --> 00:04:26,280
There's no need to worry about being killed.

61
00:04:28,450 --> 00:04:31,750
I like swinging my sword
in battle. It's my nature.

62
00:04:33,710 --> 00:04:36,750
Oh man, can you think of
anything more complicated than that?

63
00:04:37,330 --> 00:04:39,170
Corkus, you again...

64
00:04:39,170 --> 00:04:40,000
Shut up!

65
00:04:40,960 --> 00:04:42,010
Listen!

66
00:04:42,010 --> 00:04:44,300
It's a very important honor...

67
00:04:44,300 --> 00:04:47,680
Formally, the only escorts for
the fall hunt were the White Dragons...

68
00:04:47,680 --> 00:04:49,220
...the best knights in the regular army!

69
00:04:49,930 --> 00:04:53,180
In other words, we were
singled out and granted the privilege!

70
00:04:56,520 --> 00:04:59,610
We've had to run back
and forth in battle for years...

71
00:04:59,610 --> 00:05:01,730
...to reach this point and win real status.

72
00:05:01,730 --> 00:05:02,860
But you...

73
00:05:03,190 --> 00:05:04,820
How dare you call this ridiculous?

74
00:05:07,740 --> 00:05:11,290
If you love wielding your
sword so much, suit yourself!

75
00:05:39,900 --> 00:05:41,480
Do you dislike hunting?

76
00:05:59,630 --> 00:06:01,090
W-Well...

77
00:06:04,210 --> 00:06:05,710
I...

78
00:06:05,710 --> 00:06:08,090
This is my first time going hunting.

79
00:06:08,930 --> 00:06:12,220
My father compelled me to go with him...

80
00:06:14,140 --> 00:06:17,560
...but I do not think I should
like such a thing as hunting.

81
00:06:18,020 --> 00:06:19,230
It is cruel...

82
00:06:22,900 --> 00:06:24,360
So is war...

83
00:06:24,360 --> 00:06:28,530
Why do most men commit to such
affairs that only produce bloodshed?

84
00:06:37,160 --> 00:06:38,250
Oh my!

85
00:06:45,630 --> 00:06:49,130
Hold it like so,
then place it softly to your lips.

86
00:07:42,190 --> 00:07:43,850
That swollen-headed...

87
00:07:43,850 --> 00:07:45,060
Your Grace...

88
00:07:45,060 --> 00:07:46,110
Do not fuss.

89
00:07:47,110 --> 00:07:49,230
We will surely have a better opportunity.

90
00:07:49,530 --> 00:07:52,200
We had best wait for
a chance when he is alone.

91
00:07:52,950 --> 00:07:54,200
There it goes!

92
00:07:54,200 --> 00:07:55,160
Drive it into the corner!

93
00:08:01,210 --> 00:08:02,250
Don't let it get away!

94
00:08:02,250 --> 00:08:02,920
Pursue it!

95
00:08:16,550 --> 00:08:17,350
My lady!

96
00:08:18,680 --> 00:08:19,560
Hey, look!

97
00:08:50,340 --> 00:08:51,460
Whoa, whoa!

98
00:08:52,420 --> 00:08:53,130
Whoa!

99
00:08:55,130 --> 00:08:56,430
Whoa, whoa!

100
00:09:09,980 --> 00:09:12,070
Have you hurt yourself, my lady?

101
00:09:12,690 --> 00:09:14,190
We're all right, aren't we?

102
00:09:35,420 --> 00:09:36,300
My lady...

103
00:09:44,470 --> 00:09:45,680
What is the matter?

104
00:09:47,350 --> 00:09:49,980
I was scared, very scared!

105
00:09:52,400 --> 00:09:55,030
My heart is still beating so fast.

106
00:09:55,030 --> 00:09:59,240
I have never ridden a horse
so fast before in all my life.

107
00:10:02,620 --> 00:10:05,040
I can see that it's taken
your mind off things, at least.

108
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:10,210
Griffith!

109
00:10:15,210 --> 00:10:17,090
Shall we go back, my lady?

110
00:10:17,090 --> 00:10:18,630
Everyone must be worried about you.

111
00:10:46,410 --> 00:10:48,410
Griffith!

112
00:11:01,300 --> 00:11:03,010
Griffith!

113
00:11:04,180 --> 00:11:04,930
Griffith!

114
00:11:06,100 --> 00:11:06,770
Griffith!

115
00:11:06,770 --> 00:11:08,020
Captain, Captain!

116
00:11:08,480 --> 00:11:09,230
Are you all right?

117
00:11:09,770 --> 00:11:11,480
Griffith, are you all right?

118
00:11:11,480 --> 00:11:12,400
Hold on!

119
00:11:13,110 --> 00:11:14,360
Captain, hold on!

120
00:11:14,900 --> 00:11:16,070
Griffith!

121
00:11:19,650 --> 00:11:21,240
Hey, Princess!

122
00:11:22,910 --> 00:11:24,320
What's this all about?

123
00:11:24,320 --> 00:11:25,830
Where the hell
did this arrow come from?

124
00:11:26,240 --> 00:11:27,240
From where?

125
00:11:28,160 --> 00:11:29,290
You're hurting me!

126
00:11:29,290 --> 00:11:30,540
Leave me alone!

127
00:11:30,910 --> 00:11:33,540
I-I do not know... I do not...

128
00:11:34,840 --> 00:11:36,090
Not good...

129
00:11:36,090 --> 00:11:38,210
The arrow might have pierced his heart.

130
00:11:38,210 --> 00:11:38,960
No way!

131
00:11:51,060 --> 00:11:55,480
That arrow was well-poisoned with
the extract of the deadly calagile bean.

132
00:11:55,810 --> 00:11:59,570
Even a scratch will let the poison
into his blood and send him to hell.

133
00:12:00,190 --> 00:12:01,450
Griffith!

134
00:12:03,990 --> 00:12:05,780
Do not panic.

135
00:12:12,660 --> 00:12:13,460
Griffith!

136
00:12:15,380 --> 00:12:16,330
Captain!

137
00:12:17,250 --> 00:12:17,790
Hey!

138
00:12:19,130 --> 00:12:20,590
Are you really okay?

139
00:12:24,430 --> 00:12:26,090
It must be...

140
00:12:26,090 --> 00:12:27,470
...poisoned for sure.

141
00:12:28,100 --> 00:12:30,430
And a deadly poison as well...

142
00:12:30,720 --> 00:12:32,480
So how come?

143
00:12:32,810 --> 00:12:33,640
This is why.

144
00:12:34,270 --> 00:12:36,480
This served as my shield.

145
00:12:41,400 --> 00:12:43,530
The Egg of the King!

146
00:12:43,860 --> 00:12:45,160
It's that...

147
00:12:45,160 --> 00:12:47,740
...necklace you always wear.

148
00:12:47,740 --> 00:12:49,080
How can it be?

149
00:12:49,080 --> 00:12:51,080
Can it really be true?

150
00:12:51,080 --> 00:12:54,210
Wow, it's really a miracle...

151
00:12:54,210 --> 00:12:57,500
It's more like the devil's
own luck than a miracle.

152
00:12:57,880 --> 00:13:01,420
Yeah, that must be like
a talisman against evil.

153
00:13:02,460 --> 00:13:03,720
The devil's luck...

154
00:13:08,600 --> 00:13:11,010
That was some kind of luck...

155
00:13:14,680 --> 00:13:16,310
It's amazing!

156
00:13:17,230 --> 00:13:19,900
Griffith, remove your armor just in case.

157
00:13:19,900 --> 00:13:22,230
I have to see whether
you got injured or not.

158
00:13:22,230 --> 00:13:23,240
No need.

159
00:13:23,240 --> 00:13:24,400
I'm totally fine.

160
00:13:24,400 --> 00:13:25,070
No way!

161
00:13:26,740 --> 00:13:28,570
It was poisoned, wasn't it?

162
00:13:28,910 --> 00:13:31,240
What if you got a scratch
and the worst should happen?

163
00:13:34,500 --> 00:13:36,330
Believe me. I am fine.

164
00:13:36,920 --> 00:13:39,210
I escaped without
a scratch on my body.

165
00:13:39,580 --> 00:13:40,710
But if...

166
00:13:41,290 --> 00:13:43,170
E-Excuse me...

167
00:13:50,760 --> 00:13:52,180
I am sorry.

168
00:13:53,520 --> 00:13:59,520
This happened only because
I could not handle a horse...

169
00:14:03,530 --> 00:14:05,440
That is not a concern, my lady.

170
00:14:07,990 --> 00:14:11,700
It is our duty to guard you.

171
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:24,250
Who in the world intended
to kill our captain anyway?

172
00:14:24,840 --> 00:14:27,800
Wait, could he have been
aiming at the princess?

173
00:14:28,170 --> 00:14:30,010
We can't let this go either way!

174
00:14:30,010 --> 00:14:31,010
Let's kill him!

175
00:14:32,010 --> 00:14:35,850
I'll search the brush
around here with my men.

176
00:14:36,350 --> 00:14:37,430
Come on, get moving!

177
00:15:01,290 --> 00:15:02,920
It is quite expensive.

178
00:15:05,710 --> 00:15:07,340
This poison, I mean.

179
00:15:13,140 --> 00:15:14,720
How shameful!

180
00:15:15,680 --> 00:15:18,220
I sincerely apologize, but...

181
00:15:18,220 --> 00:15:20,390
I have no ears for your excuses!

182
00:15:21,350 --> 00:15:24,400
The affair has been
settled for the present...

183
00:15:24,400 --> 00:15:28,030
It's assumed Tudor's assassins
were aiming for the princess's life.

184
00:15:28,440 --> 00:15:32,070
We are virtually immune to suspicion.

185
00:15:33,280 --> 00:15:35,200
On the other hand, our actions...

186
00:15:35,200 --> 00:15:40,710
...gave Griffith credit for guarding
the princess's life with his own body.

187
00:15:42,250 --> 00:15:47,710
All the commoners began talking of
him as a hero once news got around!

188
00:15:47,710 --> 00:15:49,920
Even His Majesty is very grateful!

189
00:15:50,670 --> 00:15:54,090
Ultimately, we have helped
him increase his status!

190
00:15:54,090 --> 00:15:56,100
What a shameful situation!

191
00:15:56,430 --> 00:16:00,560
But the arrow could never
have perfectly struck his chest...

192
00:16:00,560 --> 00:16:03,690
...if the assassin was really
aiming at the princess.

193
00:16:03,900 --> 00:16:07,270
What do you think
I should do? Go and explain...

194
00:16:07,270 --> 00:16:10,780
...to His Majesty that we were merely
trying to assassinate Griffith?

195
00:16:11,360 --> 00:16:13,990
On top of all this, he's still
alive, as you well know!

196
00:16:14,360 --> 00:16:18,200
All things considered,
that was most unlikely to happen...

197
00:16:18,200 --> 00:16:19,290
Enough!

198
00:16:19,290 --> 00:16:19,910
Leave!

199
00:16:35,300 --> 00:16:36,470
His eyes...

200
00:16:38,430 --> 00:16:41,140
He looked as if he had power over me...

201
00:16:41,140 --> 00:16:43,770
As if I was a trifling thing
to be held in contempt...

202
00:16:43,770 --> 00:16:45,900
That look was in his eyes.

203
00:16:47,520 --> 00:16:48,860
Nonsense!

204
00:16:48,860 --> 00:16:50,480
I am royalty!

205
00:16:50,480 --> 00:16:53,700
I even have a claim to the throne!

206
00:16:53,700 --> 00:16:55,910
Regarding my status and class...

207
00:16:55,910 --> 00:16:59,240
...I am worlds apart from
that man of common birth.

208
00:16:59,240 --> 00:17:00,240
Nevertheless...

209
00:17:00,620 --> 00:17:02,250
I've seen that look before...

210
00:17:03,040 --> 00:17:07,210
For a moment, his eyes seemed
to be a beast's focusing on prey...

211
00:17:07,750 --> 00:17:08,750
Yes!

212
00:17:08,750 --> 00:17:11,670
He gazed at me the way
a hawk would gaze at prey...

213
00:17:16,130 --> 00:17:17,340
Is it because...

214
00:17:17,840 --> 00:17:19,800
No, that cannot be.

215
00:17:19,800 --> 00:17:22,600
There were many
other feudal lords nearby.

216
00:17:22,600 --> 00:17:25,520
I just met his gaze for a moment...

217
00:17:25,520 --> 00:17:28,310
Firstly, there was no evidence of it...

218
00:17:32,690 --> 00:17:33,780
He couldn't...

219
00:18:05,310 --> 00:18:06,310
Hey...

220
00:18:11,900 --> 00:18:13,190
Thanks for coming.

221
00:18:13,730 --> 00:18:15,360
Can you wait a moment?

222
00:18:15,360 --> 00:18:17,070
I'll finish up everything soon.

223
00:18:19,030 --> 00:18:20,490
It keeps on growing.

224
00:18:24,660 --> 00:18:26,200
Have you read them all?

225
00:18:26,200 --> 00:18:28,000
Well, yes, almost.

226
00:18:28,960 --> 00:18:33,340
When you become so distinguished,
you must do more than battle.

227
00:18:34,130 --> 00:18:37,380
Well, I really just read
them out of mere curiosity.

228
00:18:38,590 --> 00:18:43,220
History, religion,
philosophy, chemistry, tactics...

229
00:18:44,060 --> 00:18:48,640
There is even a book on applying
makeup and a book on cooking...

230
00:18:48,640 --> 00:18:49,940
...there are so many...

231
00:18:51,900 --> 00:18:54,360
So what's the problem?

232
00:19:21,800 --> 00:19:25,810
I want to ask you to kill a man for me.

233
00:19:53,540 --> 00:19:54,880
Kill a man?

234
00:19:54,880 --> 00:19:55,460
Who?

235
00:19:56,790 --> 00:19:59,670
The man who is next in line
to the throne of Midland...

236
00:19:59,670 --> 00:20:01,880
...the general of the White Dragons, Count Julius.

237
00:20:05,300 --> 00:20:06,430
The reason...

238
00:20:07,310 --> 00:20:08,510
...is this!

239
00:20:10,850 --> 00:20:14,940
This arrow was poisoned with the
essence of the deadly calagile bean.

240
00:20:16,360 --> 00:20:19,480
No ordinary person would
ever have a use for such a bean.

241
00:20:20,990 --> 00:20:24,990
Only one man has purchased
this deadly poison recently...

242
00:20:25,820 --> 00:20:29,740
He is the best archer in the
White Dragons, a man named Hail.

243
00:20:30,790 --> 00:20:34,420
I paid off an attendant
to help smell out the plot.

244
00:20:34,420 --> 00:20:38,090
She reported that she saw that
man come out of Julius's office...

245
00:20:38,090 --> 00:20:41,170
...this evening, right after he got
a good scolding from the general.

246
00:20:44,180 --> 00:20:45,840
This is an assassination.

247
00:20:46,510 --> 00:20:49,720
It could not be more
different than fighting in battle.

248
00:20:51,770 --> 00:20:55,600
It's a dirty task, and failure will never be allowed.

249
00:20:57,520 --> 00:20:59,650
You must not be seen either.

250
00:21:01,360 --> 00:21:05,150
On account of the difficulty, I am
asking if you would undertake the task.

251
00:21:06,280 --> 00:21:08,240
Will you undertake it for me?

252
00:21:13,660 --> 00:21:14,870
This is not like you.

253
00:21:16,420 --> 00:21:20,880
You should just order me to do it,
without saying all this other crap.

254
00:22:03,390 --> 00:22:05,850
Looking back, the morning comes.

255
00:22:05,850 --> 00:22:09,350
Don't find your face in your glass.

256
00:22:10,390 --> 00:22:13,480
Take the moonlight by the tail.

257
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:16,440
It's a rainy sight. You're shading.

258
00:22:17,900 --> 00:22:19,650
What is that?

259
00:22:19,650 --> 00:22:20,900
It's just the same.

260
00:22:20,900 --> 00:22:24,070
What is trying your crown?

261
00:22:25,160 --> 00:22:28,370
I'm spending my glass, walking back.

262
00:22:28,370 --> 00:22:31,410
So wear my glass. You're fading.

263
00:22:31,710 --> 00:22:51,310
I'm waiting so long.

264
00:22:51,310 --> 00:23:00,400
I'm waiting...

